      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale for the note field. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
