       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day of metformin is twice the maximum labeled daily dose, and I can't think of a clinical situation where that's appropriate. The risk to the patient is serious, mainly lactic acidosis. A confirmation alone doesn't change that, and you haven't given a rationale.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** Give me the dose and frequency, for example 850 mg three times daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or the attending.** If there's a reason for this dose that I don't know about, they can review it and enter it through their own process.\n- **Check the source.** If this came from a transcription or a template, it may be worth verifying the original."
